  "content": {
    "id": "p30-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Find the values of $x$ for which:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p30-q3a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^3+2x^2-9x-18\\le0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\le-3$ or $-2\\le x\\le3$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^3+2x^2-9x-18&=x^2(x+2)-9(x+2)\\\\x^3+2x^2-9x-18&=(x+2)(x-3)(x+3).\\end{align*}$$\nThe zeroes are $-3,-2,3$, all simple. With positive leading coefficient, the graph is below the axis for $x<-3$ and $-2<x<3$. Including the zeroes gives $x\\le-3$ or $-2\\le x\\le3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q3b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$2x^3+x^2-8x-4>0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-2<x<-\\frac12$ or $x>2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2x^3+x^2-8x-4&=x^2(2x+1)-4(2x+1)\\\\2x^3+x^2-8x-4&=(2x+1)(x-2)(x+2).\\end{align*}$$\nThe simple zeroes are $-2,-\\frac12,2$. The leading coefficient is positive, so the graph is above the axis for $-2<x<-\\frac12$ and $x>2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q3c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$x^3-x^2<5x+3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<-1$ or $-1<x<3$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^3-x^2-5x-3&<0\\\\(x+1)^2(x-3)&<0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe graph touches the axis at $-1$ and crosses at $3$. It is below the axis for $x<3$, except at $-1$. Hence $x<-1$ or $-1<x<3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q3d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$x^4+3x^2\\ge3x^3+x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\le0$ or $x\\ge1$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^4-3x^3+3x^2-x&\\ge0\\\\x(x-1)^3&\\ge0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe graph crosses at $0$ and $1$ and has positive leading coefficient. It is above the axis for $x<0$ and $x>1$. Including the zeroes gives $x\\le0$ or $x\\ge1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      }
    ]
  },
